{
 "schema": 1,
 "generator": "scripts/art/blender/penitent.mjs (Blender 4.2.3 + scripts/art/blender/penitent.py, gltf-transform 4.5.1)",
 "provenance": "ORIGINAL: modelled and textured in code by this project (no third-party mesh or texture); docs/ASSET-PROVENANCE.md section 5",
 "pathsRelativeTo": "public/ (at runtime: import.meta.env.BASE_URL + path, e.g. loadAssetContainer(scene, file))",
 "space": "Rigid pieces: glTF model space of the UBC/Outfit 65-joint rig at REST (right-handed, +Y up, faces +Z, rig units = metres before the actor's root scale), translated so each file's origin is its bone's rest position. Censer: world metres for the 2.52 m Penitent.",
 "rig": {
  "primary": "regular-male",
  "supported": [
   "regular-male",
   "ubc-superhero-male"
  ],
  "fingerprints": {
   "regular-male": "422d169e89",
   "ubc-superhero-male": "d55444f030"
  },
  "why": "regular-male is the rig of the male outfits (Male_Peasant / Male_Ranger + Superhero_Male_Head), the natural body under the armour; ubc-superhero-male (Superhero_Male_FullBody) differs only at the arms, hands and thighs (2-3 cm wider) and uses attachByRig. Pieces are bone-relative, so they follow either rig's joints."
 },
 "howToAttach": [
  "Load each file with loadAssetContainer; skip the loader's __root__ (it only converts glTF to Babylon's left-handed space) and parent each node listed in `nodes` to the body's joint TransformNode named `bone` (glTF joints are TransformNodes under the body's own __root__). A single-material node loads as a Mesh; a multi-material one (gauntlets, vambraces, faulds, tassets, cuirass rivets) as a node whose children are the per-material meshes: parent that node. tests/assets/penitent.test.ts proves this recipe in Babylon against Male_Peasant.glb.",
  "Set node.position = attach.position, node.rotationQuaternion = attach.rotation (x, y, z, w), node.scaling = attach.scale. Values are in glTF space, the space joint TransformNodes live in. attach.rotation = inverse(bone rest world rotation), so the piece lands exactly where it was modelled at rest and then follows the bone.",
  "Every piece follows its bone rigidly; the actor's root scale (2.52 m Penitent) applies through the skeleton, so pieces need no scale of their own.",
  "Alternative with 4 draw calls instead of 24 (each multi-material piece loads as one mesh per material): penitent_armour_skinned.glb holds the same pieces as one skinned mesh per material bound to the regular-male bind pose (every vertex weight 1.0 to its piece's bone); bind it to the body's skeleton like the outfit accessories.",
  "Materials come from the GLB (PBRMaterial): call applyLightBudget on each; the mist plugin attaches automatically. All are doubleSided (thin plates, open lames).",
  "Fallback: if any file fails to load, keep the procedural Penitent (render/actors/penitent.ts); nothing here is required for gameplay."
 ],
